AcceptanceCriteria.Criterion:
Caret memory: typing in the source pane while the rich
    pane's caret sits mid-document does not move the rich caret's
    remembered position (re-mapped and clamped into the updated text);
    alt-tabbing focus between panes restores each surface's own caret;
    IME composition in a pane is never broken by the other pane's
    updates.

NonGoals.NonGoal:
Changing what full-window Source Code mode or WYSIWYG mode
    means without split (their single-surface behavior is unchanged;
    only the split combination becomes dual-editable).
